{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_060790fa73c3100b806c41c281d3bb198d3bd188552f8eb7c78aeb7c861024b7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented Ollama qwen3 streaming shows tool_calls arriving complete within a single data chunk, including function name and arguments, requiring no extra concatenation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3f44cddc2217087654c456e7aae24a3c4d2aed998e00751b5c57c125b1d35272"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented DeepSeek-R1 streaming separates reasoning into a reasoning_content delta field (with reasoning_tokens counted in usage) before regular content deltas begin."},{"claim_ids":["clm_599285ba2a501176851a2d026b93ac9a935e92d3c18b9fb5b12a562e24ec09a0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"APIResponse.md documents that Ollama's deepseek-r1 streams thinking and answer content together in the content field, with thinking wrapped in <think> tags, unlike qwen3 which places reasoning in a separate thinking field."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ea91459b1cab32bd760589d68b637d652dc0cbf82650cdc5d50138f1edf6d45c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented OpenAI streaming tool calls arrive incrementally: each delta carries a tool_calls fragment with index, id, function name, and argument string split across chunks, finishing with finish_reason 'tool_calls'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ebe75ac29d72bd2d2e16c6354077482d665bd0bf24bd0daa67438f280d30e459"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented OpenAI streaming responses use SSE 'data:' chunks of chat.completion.chunk objects; the finish_reason stop chunk is followed by a separate chunk with empty choices that carries usage, then a 'data: [DONE]' sentinel."}],"claim_ids":["clm_060790fa73c3100b806c41c281d3bb198d3bd188552f8eb7c78aeb7c861024b7","clm_3f44cddc2217087654c456e7aae24a3c4d2aed998e00751b5c57c125b1d35272","clm_599285ba2a501176851a2d026b93ac9a935e92d3c18b9fb5b12a562e24ec09a0","clm_ea91459b1cab32bd760589d68b637d652dc0cbf82650cdc5d50138f1edf6d45c","clm_ebe75ac29d72bd2d2e16c6354077482d665bd0bf24bd0daa67438f280d30e459"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5c99e8d705d04e0d956ec1eadac172b1","id":"pg_98288a3b21fc5dfb89d928d4c4208895","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/lnyo-cly-ai4j-apiresponse-md-ba6b79738535-28d4c4208895.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_21b0b230c0485880b30ff8e550a6b4f3"],"title":"LnYo-Cly/ai4j/APIResponse.md @ ba6b79738535","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5c99e8d705d04e0d956ec1eadac172b1"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_07759a5cd6b185b62c473dc2eb8a5d6ff6cb2daafdf35e419523877dbb8b05e8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ai4j is described as a Java AI agentic development kit targeting JDK 8+, unifying model access, tool calling, MCP, A2A, RAG, an agent runtime, and a built-in coding agent CLI/TUI/ACP."},{"claim_ids":["clm_35bee78282a7d8ee3daf4ae6bc8a57353fcfe2f9d824ba90f3fb0ee1486f9e26"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Switching providers such as DashScope, DeepSeek, or Ollama is presented as changing only the PlatformType and corresponding config object while the rest of the calling code stays unchanged."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5d49783e73b207a9c4204d3e5846d40121294cb6f098bb332932a53643da535d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The library is published as io.github.lnyo-cly:ai4j version 2.4.2, installable via Gradle or Maven dependency declarations."},{"claim_ids":["clm_952fc25793abeafe9773dc4a4b4010bb176208e945ff9c3e517c55da72f0e0e3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The quickstart flow: build an OpenAiConfig with an API key from OPENAI_API_KEY, wrap it in a Configuration, obtain an IChatService from AiService via PlatformType.OPENAI, then send a ChatCompletion built with a model name and user message."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b85a30327e058ec9ea787a242a7399706ec90e7de41e3215aa47601639beb550"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Supported platforms listed include OpenAI and compatible APIs, Anthropic, DashScope, Doubao, DeepSeek, Moonshot, Zhipu, Hunyuan, Lingyi, Ollama, MiniMax, Baichuan, and Suno, plus rerank providers, AgentFlow (Dify/Coze/n8n), and vector stores (Pinecone, Qdrant, pgvector, Milvus, Redis)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c760938c3b0a83108dcddfa13dc926a4fd65f483edf40fe75c8c0c4487448d11"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is licensed under Apache License 2.0 and links to a GitHub Pages documentation site plus guides for the coding agent CLI and A2A protocol."}],"claim_ids":["clm_07759a5cd6b185b62c473dc2eb8a5d6ff6cb2daafdf35e419523877dbb8b05e8","clm_35bee78282a7d8ee3daf4ae6bc8a57353fcfe2f9d824ba90f3fb0ee1486f9e26","clm_5d49783e73b207a9c4204d3e5846d40121294cb6f098bb332932a53643da535d","clm_952fc25793abeafe9773dc4a4b4010bb176208e945ff9c3e517c55da72f0e0e3","clm_b85a30327e058ec9ea787a242a7399706ec90e7de41e3215aa47601639beb550","clm_c760938c3b0a83108dcddfa13dc926a4fd65f483edf40fe75c8c0c4487448d11"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5c99e8d705d04e0d956ec1eadac172b1","id":"pg_9c446d626b595726ac73646f11f36f3a","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/lnyo-cly-ai4j-readme-md-ba6b79738535-646f11f36f3a.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_589b0b9aeaec5845bf3b6d97ff43f395"],"title":"LnYo-Cly/ai4j/README.md @ ba6b79738535","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5c99e8d705d04e0d956ec1eadac172b1"}
